---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Probe56CTA from '../components/Probe56CTA.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const tiers = [
  {
    name: 'Probe56 Open Source',
    label: 'Free',
    cta: 'Get Started Free',
    ctaHref: '#free-scan',
    ctaExternal: false,
    highlight: false,
    features: ['Probe56 CLI', 'Element scanning', 'P56 bundle format', 'MIT license', 'Any HuggingFace model'],
  },
  {
    name: 'GI X-Ray',
    label: 'Contact Us',
    cta: 'Contact Us',
    ctaHref: 'mailto:yonathan@growing-intelligence.com?subject=GI X-Ray Request',
    ctaExternal: false,
    highlight: true,
    features: ['Full 56-element scan', 'Layer-by-layer analysis', 'Anomaly heatmap', 'Hallucination risk report', 'Signed PDF delivery', 'Email in 24h'],
  },
  {
    name: 'GI Monitor',
    label: 'Contact Us',
    cta: 'Contact Us',
    ctaHref: 'mailto:yonathan@growing-intelligence.com?subject=GI Monitor Inquiry',
    ctaExternal: false,
    highlight: false,
    features: ['Real-time drift detection', 'Element composition alerts', 'Dashboard access', 'Monthly summary report', 'Up to 3 models', 'Slack/PagerDuty integration'],
  },
  {
    name: 'GI Surgeon',
    label: 'Request a Quote',
    cta: 'Request a Quote',
    ctaHref: 'mailto:yonathan@growing-intelligence.com?subject=GI Surgeon Inquiry',
    ctaExternal: false,
    highlight: false,
    features: ['Targeted model editing', 'Validated hallucination fix', '50-prompt regression suite', 'Minimal perplexity impact', 'Air-gap deployment', 'Enterprise contract'],
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Probe56 — AI Model Scanning"
  description="Scan your AI model with the Holosynthics periodic table. Open-source Python CLI, managed X-Ray analysis, real-time monitoring, and surgical editing."
>
  <Nav />

  <main class="df-page">
    <!-- Hero -->
    <section class="df-hero">
      <div class="hero-glow"></div>
      <div class="df-hero-inner">
        <div class="badge">Developer Tools</div>
        <h1>Scan Any AI Model.<br /><span class="accent">Understand Every Element.</span></h1>
        <p>Probe56 scans your model's element composition. GI X-Ray maps it to the 56-element periodic table. GI Surgeon fixes what's broken — without retraining.</p>

        <div class="quickstart">
          <code>pip install probe56 && probe56 scan --model gpt2 --output my_model.p56</code>
        </div>

        <div class="df-actions">
          <a href="#tools" class="btn-primary">See All Tools</a>
        </div>

        <div class="hero-stats">
          <div class="hero-stat"><span class="hs-num">56</span><span class="hs-label">Elements</span></div>
          <div class="hero-stat-sep">|</div>
          <div class="hero-stat"><span class="hs-num">13</span><span class="hs-label">Families</span></div>
          <div class="hero-stat-sep">|</div>
          <div class="hero-stat"><span class="hs-num">5</span><span class="hs-label">Repair Dimensions</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- How it works -->
    <section class="how-section" id="how">
      <div class="container">
        <h2>How It Works</h2>
        <div class="steps-grid">
          <div class="hw-step">
            <div class="hw-num">01</div>
            <h3>Extract</h3>
            <p>Probe56 (open-source Python CLI) scans your model during inference and captures element composition data from your dataset.</p>
            <code>probe56 scan --model your/model --dataset truthfulqa</code>
          </div>
          <div class="hw-step">
            <div class="hw-num">02</div>
            <h3>Bundle</h3>
            <p>Scan data is compressed into a P56 bundle — a signed, deterministic binary format with cryptographic hash of the model weights. Portable, verifiable.</p>
            <code>→ scan_bundle.p56 (SHA-256 verified)</code>
          </div>
          <div class="hw-step">
            <div class="hw-num">03</div>
            <h3>Analyze</h3>
            <p>GI X-Ray maps your bundle against the Holosynthics 56-element periodic table. Produces a heatmap of which elements dominate which layers, and flags anomalies.</p>
            <code>→ 56-element report + anomaly score</code>
          </div>
          <div class="hw-step">
            <div class="hw-num">04</div>
            <h3>Repair (optional)</h3>
            <p>GI Surgeon applies precision edits to the identified problem areas. No retraining. Fully reversible. Validated against regression suite.</p>
            <code>→ patched model weights</code>
            <div class="quote-block">
              <span class="quote-text">Want to fix these issues?</span>
              <a href="mailto:yonathan@growing-intelligence.com?subject=Get a Quote" class="quote-link">Get a quote &rarr;</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- GI X-Ray section -->
    <section class="tool-detail" id="tools">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="tool-detail-inner">
          <div class="tool-text">
            <span class="tool-label">GI X-Ray</span>
            <h2>See Your Model's Element Map</h2>
            <p>Send us your Probe56 bundle. We run the full 56-element analysis and return a comprehensive report showing which elements dominate the composition, where anomalies concentrate, and what your hallucination risk profile looks like.</p>
            <ul class="feature-list">
              <li>Full periodic table heatmap per layer</li>
              <li>Anomaly cluster identification</li>
              <li>Entropy.Confidence trace (hallucination predictor)</li>
              <li>Cross-model comparison</li>
              <li>Signed PDF report + raw JSON data</li>
            </ul>
            <a href="mailto:yonathan@growing-intelligence.com?subject=GI X-Ray Request" class="btn-request">Contact Us for a Scan &rarr;</a>
            <div class="quote-block">
              <span class="quote-text">Want to fix these issues?</span>
              <a href="mailto:yonathan@growing-intelligence.com?subject=Get a Quote" class="quote-link">Get a quote &rarr;</a>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="tool-visual xray-visual">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 300 200" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-label="X-Ray heatmap diagram">
              <rect width="300" height="200" fill="#0D0F23" rx="12"/>
              <text x="150" y="24" fill="#8892A4" font-size="10" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Inter,sans-serif">Layer Distribution Heatmap</text>
              {Array.from({length: 8}, (_, col) =>
                Array.from({length: 7}, (_, row) => {
                  const colors = ['#F72585','#00D9FF','#7209B7','#4CC9F0','#22C55E','#FFD60A','#F59E0B','#EF4444'];
                  const vals = [0.5, 0.8, 0.3, 0.6, 0.4, 0.7, 0.9, 0.2];
                  const opacity = Math.max(0.1, Math.min(0.95, vals[(col + row) % 8]));
                  return `<rect x="${30 + col*32}" y="${36 + row*22}" width="28" height="18" rx="3" fill="${colors[col]}" opacity="${opacity.toFixed(2)}"/>`;
                }).join('')
              ).join('')}
              <text x="150" y="195" fill="#8892A4" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Inter,sans-serif">Bo · Nu · Sy · Id · Sp · Ti · Re · En</text>
            </svg>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- GI Monitor section -->
    <section class="tool-detail alt" id="monitor">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="tool-detail-inner reverse">
          <div class="tool-text">
            <span class="tool-label">GI Monitor</span>
            <h2>Track Element Drift in Real Time</h2>
            <p>As models are updated, fine-tuned, or exposed to distribution shifts, their element composition changes. GI Monitor detects these changes before they manifest as output degradation.</p>
            <ul class="feature-list">
              <li>Continuous element composition tracking</li>
              <li>Drift alerts before output quality degrades</li>
              <li>Slack and PagerDuty integration</li>
              <li>Monthly composition summary</li>
              <li>Comparison across model versions</li>
            </ul>
            <a href="mailto:yonathan@growing-intelligence.com?subject=GI Monitor Inquiry" class="btn-request">Contact Us &rarr;</a>
          </div>
          <div class="tool-visual monitor-visual">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 300 200" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-label="Monitor drift diagram">
              <rect width="300" height="200" fill="#0D0F23" rx="12"/>
              <text x="150" y="20" fill="#8892A4" font-size="10" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Inter,sans-serif">Element Composition Over Time</text>
              <!-- Stable line -->
              <polyline points="20,80 60,78 100,82 140,79 180,81 220,76 260,80 280,78" fill="none" stroke="#00D9FF" stroke-width="2" opacity="0.8"/>
              <!-- Drift line -->
              <polyline points="180,81 200,90 220,105 240,118 260,130 280,140" fill="none" stroke="#EF4444" stroke-width="2" opacity="0.8"/>
              <!-- Alert marker -->
              <circle cx="200" cy="90" r="5" fill="#FFD60A" opacity="0.9"/>
              <text x="206" y="88" fill="#FFD60A" font-size="8" font-family="Inter,sans-serif">drift detected</text>
              <!-- Legend -->
              <rect x="20" y="160" width="12" height="3" fill="#00D9FF"/>
              <text x="36" y="164" fill="#8892A4" font-size="8" font-family="Inter,sans-serif">stable</text>
              <rect x="80" y="160" width="12" height="3" fill="#EF4444"/>
              <text x="96" y="164" fill="#8892A4" font-size="8" font-family="Inter,sans-serif">drift detected</text>
            </svg>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- GI Surgeon section -->
    <section class="tool-detail" id="surgeon">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="tool-detail-inner">
          <div class="tool-text">
            <span class="tool-label">GI Surgeon</span>
            <h2>Fix Hallucinations Without Retraining</h2>
            <p>GI Surgeon identifies the specific element patterns responsible for a hallucination and applies precision edits — validated, reversible, no retraining required.</p>
            <ul class="feature-list">
              <li>Precision edits (permanent, reversible)</li>
              <li>Validated correction, zero regressions</li>
              <li>50-prompt regression suite before every commit</li>
              <li>Minimal perplexity impact (validated)</li>
              <li>Air-gap deployment available</li>
            </ul>
            <a href="mailto:yonathan@growing-intelligence.com?subject=GI Surgeon Inquiry" class="btn-request">Request a Quote &rarr;</a>
            <div class="quote-block">
              <span class="quote-text">Want to fix these issues?</span>
              <a href="mailto:yonathan@growing-intelligence.com?subject=Get a Quote" class="quote-link">Get a quote &rarr;</a>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="tool-visual surgeon-visual">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 300 200" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-label="Element map diagram">
              <rect width="300" height="200" fill="#0D0F23" rx="12"/>
              <text x="60" y="24" fill="#8892A4" font-size="10" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Inter,sans-serif">BEFORE</text>
              <text x="210" y="24" fill="#8892A4" font-size="10" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Inter,sans-serif">AFTER</text>
              <!-- Noise bar (before) -->
              <rect x="20" y="36" width="80" height="12" rx="2" fill="#7209B7" opacity="0.9"/>
              <text x="24" y="46" fill="#fff" font-size="7" font-family="Inter,sans-serif">Symbol.General (noise)</text>
              <!-- Signal bar (before) — small -->
              <rect x="20" y="56" width="30" height="12" rx="2" fill="#FFD60A" opacity="0.6"/>
              <text x="24" y="66" fill="#fff" font-size="7" font-family="Inter,sans-serif">Time.Era (weak)</text>
              <!-- Arrow -->
              <text x="150" y="80" fill="#00D9FF" font-size="24" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Inter,sans-serif">&#8594;</text>
              <text x="150" y="100" fill="#8892A4" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Inter,sans-serif">GI Surgeon</text>
              <!-- Noise bar (after) — suppressed -->
              <rect x="170" y="36" width="25" height="12" rx="2" fill="#7209B7" opacity="0.35"/>
              <text x="174" y="46" fill="#fff" font-size="7" font-family="Inter,sans-serif">Symbol (suppressed)</text>
              <!-- Signal bar (after) — amplified -->
              <rect x="170" y="56" width="95" height="12" rx="2" fill="#FFD60A" opacity="0.9"/>
              <text x="174" y="66" fill="#fff" font-size="7" font-family="Inter,sans-serif">Time.Era (amplified)</text>
              <!-- Result -->
              <rect x="20" y="120" width="260" height="20" rx="4" fill="#22C55E" opacity="0.15"/>
              <rect x="20" y="120" width="260" height="20" rx="4" fill="none" stroke="#22C55E" stroke-width="1" opacity="0.4"/>
              <text x="150" y="134" fill="#22C55E" font-size="10" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Inter,sans-serif">Output: correct — no retraining</text>
              <text x="150" y="165" fill="#8892A4" font-size="8" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Inter,sans-serif">Fully reversible. Regression passed. Permanent.</text>
            </svg>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 5 Dimensions of AI Model Health -->
    <section class="dims-section" id="dimensions">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="dims-header">
          <div class="results-badge">What We Measure</div>
          <h2>5 Dimensions of AI Model Health</h2>
          <p class="results-sub">Every Probe56 scan scores your model across five dimensions. A weak score in any one of them predicts where failures will appear in production.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="dims-grid">
          <div class="dim-card" style="--dc: #00D9FF">
            <div class="dim-icon">🔍</div>
            <h3>Knowledge</h3>
            <p>The AI knows factual information correctly and does not invent facts it was never trained on.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="dim-card" style="--dc: #F59E0B">
            <div class="dim-icon">⚙️</div>
            <h3>Reasoning</h3>
            <p>The AI draws logically valid conclusions from premises — cause and effect, if-then, because.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="dim-card" style="--dc: #22C55E">
            <div class="dim-icon">🛠</div>
            <h3>Skills</h3>
            <p>The AI can perform tasks accurately — translation, coding, summarization, calculation.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="dim-card" style="--dc: #7209B7">
            <div class="dim-icon">📐</div>
            <h3>Logical Generalization</h3>
            <p>The AI applies rules consistently across new cases it has not seen before during training.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="dim-card" style="--dc: #EF4444">
            <div class="dim-icon">⚖️</div>
            <h3>Judgment</h3>
            <p>The AI makes sound decisions under uncertainty and knows the limits of what it knows.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Benchmark Foundation Mini -->
    <section class="bmini-section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="bmini-header">
          <div class="results-badge">Validation Foundation</div>
          <h2>Validated Against 1.8M Academic Benchmarks</h2>
          <p class="bmini-sub">Every scan runs 8 fixed categories — peer-reviewed datasets, zero auto-generated questions.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bmini-grid">
          <div class="bmini-card" style="--bc: #00D9FF">
            <span class="bmini-icon">🔍</span>
            <div class="bmini-name">General Knowledge</div>
            <div class="bmini-count">58,934</div>
            <div class="bmini-bm">MMLU · HellaSwag · TriviaQA</div>
          </div>
          <div class="bmini-card" style="--bc: #818CF8">
            <span class="bmini-icon">🧠</span>
            <div class="bmini-name">Reasoning</div>
            <div class="bmini-count">869,978</div>
            <div class="bmini-bm">BBH · ProofWriter · EntailmentBank</div>
          </div>
          <div class="bmini-card" style="--bc: #FB923C">
            <span class="bmini-icon">⚡</span>
            <div class="bmini-name">Logic</div>
            <div class="bmini-count">1,151</div>
            <div class="bmini-bm">LogiQA · ReClor</div>
          </div>
          <div class="bmini-card" style="--bc: #34D399">
            <span class="bmini-icon">📐</span>
            <div class="bmini-name">Mathematics</div>
            <div class="bmini-count">7,158</div>
            <div class="bmini-bm">GSM8K · MATH-500 · TheoremQA</div>
          </div>
          <div class="bmini-card" style="--bc: #60A5FA">
            <span class="bmini-icon">💡</span>
            <div class="bmini-name">Commonsense</div>
            <div class="bmini-count">17,277</div>
            <div class="bmini-bm">PIQA · SocialIQA · XCOPA</div>
          </div>
          <div class="bmini-card" style="--bc: #F472B6">
            <span class="bmini-icon">🎯</span>
            <div class="bmini-name">Hallucination</div>
            <div class="bmini-count">5,143</div>
            <div class="bmini-bm">TruthfulQA · SimpleQA</div>
          </div>
          <div class="bmini-card" style="--bc: #F87171">
            <span class="bmini-icon">🛡️</span>
            <div class="bmini-name">Safety</div>
            <div class="bmini-count">157,934</div>
            <div class="bmini-bm">BBQ · RealToxicityPrompts</div>
          </div>
          <div class="bmini-card" style="--bc: #A3E635">
            <span class="bmini-icon">📖</span>
            <div class="bmini-name">Reading Comprehension</div>
            <div class="bmini-count">28,075</div>
            <div class="bmini-bm">SQuAD · DROP · BoolQ</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="bmini-cta-row">
          <a href="/benchmarks" class="bmini-cta-link">See all 46 categories — 1,801,476 questions →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Surgeon Results — 4-way comparison -->
    <section class="results-section" id="results">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="results-header">
          <div class="results-badge">Proven Results</div>
          <h2>GI Surgeon vs. the Field</h2>
          <p class="results-sub">Benchmarks run against CounterFact and RippleEdits. Every result is Ed25519 signed and independently reproducible.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="results-table">
          <div class="rt-row rt-head">
            <div class="rt-metric">Metric</div>
            <div class="rt-ours">GI Surgeon</div>
            <div class="rt-b1">ROME</div>
            <div class="rt-b2">AlphaEdit</div>
            <div class="rt-b3">MEMIT</div>
          </div>
          <div class="rt-row">
            <div class="rt-metric">Neighborhood Score (NS)</div>
            <div class="rt-ours win">83.4%</div>
            <div class="rt-b1">78.2%</div>
            <div class="rt-b2">75.48%</div>
            <div class="rt-b3">73.7%</div>
          </div>
          <div class="rt-row">
            <div class="rt-metric">Architectures supported</div>
            <div class="rt-ours win">13</div>
            <div class="rt-b1">2–3</div>
            <div class="rt-b2">2–3</div>
            <div class="rt-b3">2–3</div>
          </div>
          <div class="rt-row">
            <div class="rt-metric">Side effects on neighbors</div>
            <div class="rt-ours win">0</div>
            <div class="rt-b1">unverified</div>
            <div class="rt-b2">unverified</div>
            <div class="rt-b3">unverified</div>
          </div>
          <div class="rt-row">
            <div class="rt-metric">Cryptographically signed proof</div>
            <div class="rt-ours win">Yes</div>
            <div class="rt-b1">No</div>
            <div class="rt-b2">No</div>
            <div class="rt-b3">No</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="results-note">Method protected by provisional patents filed with the USPTO.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Two-Layer Repair Explainer -->
    <section class="repair-section" id="repair">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="results-header">
          <div class="results-badge">How Repair Works</div>
          <h2>Two-Layer Repair</h2>
          <p class="results-sub">One repair pass fixes the obvious problems. Two passes fix what's hiding underneath — without touching anything that already works.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="repair-flow">
          <div class="rf-step">
            <div class="rf-num">1</div>
            <div class="rf-title">Scan</div>
            <div class="rf-desc">We scan your model and get a full map of what's broken and where.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="rf-arrow">&rarr;</div>
          <div class="rf-step">
            <div class="rf-num">2</div>
            <div class="rf-title">Fix</div>
            <div class="rf-desc">We fix the highest-priority issues with targeted edits. No retraining.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="rf-arrow">&rarr;</div>
          <div class="rf-step">
            <div class="rf-num">3</div>
            <div class="rf-title">Scan again</div>
            <div class="rf-desc">We re-scan the repaired model to expose what the first pass uncovered.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="rf-arrow">&rarr;</div>
          <div class="rf-step">
            <div class="rf-num">4</div>
            <div class="rf-title">Fix again</div>
            <div class="rf-desc">Second layer of repairs targets the newly visible issues.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="rf-arrow">&rarr;</div>
          <div class="rf-step rf-final">
            <div class="rf-num">5</div>
            <div class="rf-title">Prove</div>
            <div class="rf-desc">Cryptographically signed before-and-after report. Every fix is auditable.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="repair-cta">
          <span>Want this for your model?</span>
          <a href="mailto:yonathan@growing-intelligence.com?subject=Get a Quote" class="quote-link">Get a quote &rarr;</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Case Study -->
    <section class="case-section" id="case-study">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="results-header">
          <div class="results-badge">Real Results</div>
          <h2>Case Study: Medical AI Provider</h2>
          <p class="results-sub">A real product run. Numbers from the signed report. Nothing fabricated.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="case-grid">
          <div class="case-story">
            <p>A medical AI provider's model was showing unexpected behavior on clinical knowledge questions. They ran a Probe56 scan, then a GI Surgeon repair cycle.</p>
            <p>The scan found 78 anomalous element patterns across the model. Most were structural — they're how every model works. Two were fixable without retraining.</p>
            <p>After the Two-Layer Repair: both target behaviors corrected, all 20 preserved behaviors still passing, zero side effects detected in the regression suite.</p>
            <p class="case-fingerprint">Report fingerprint: <code>a9c492a3…</code> &middot; Ed25519 signed</p>
          </div>
          <div class="case-stats">
            <div class="cs-row">
              <div class="cs-label">Probe56 health score</div>
              <div class="cs-before">1.2%</div>
              <div class="cs-arrow">&rarr;</div>
              <div class="cs-after">2.5%</div>
            </div>
            <div class="cs-row">
              <div class="cs-label">Issues found</div>
              <div class="cs-val">78</div>
            </div>
            <div class="cs-row">
              <div class="cs-label">Fixable at weight level</div>
              <div class="cs-val">2</div>
            </div>
            <div class="cs-row cs-win">
              <div class="cs-label">Fixed (no retraining)</div>
              <div class="cs-val">2 / 2</div>
            </div>
            <div class="cs-row cs-win">
              <div class="cs-label">Preserved behaviors</div>
              <div class="cs-val">20 / 20</div>
            </div>
            <div class="cs-row cs-win">
              <div class="cs-label">Side effects</div>
              <div class="cs-val">0</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>


    <!-- Registration -->
    <section class="reg-section" id="free-scan">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="reg-inner">
          <div class="reg-text">
            <h2>Get Your Free Scan Report</h2>
